WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.600
Speaker 1: Could the coming 2022 midterm election&nbsp;
be the worst midterm ever for Republicans?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.880
In this particular situation, the situation being&nbsp;
one that should be very good for the Republican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.200
Party if you look historically. I know many of you&nbsp;
are sick of hearing this from me, but I want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:24.480
remind everybody. Normally, when one party takes&nbsp;
the White House from the other party in the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:31.680
midterm election, after that, that very party then&nbsp;
loses a bunch of seats or potentially control of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:37.200
the House or Senate. Meaning because Democrats&nbsp;
took the White House from Republicans in 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:43.600
2022 should be very, very good for Republicans.&nbsp;
And it was looking that way for a very long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.360
time. And all of a sudden in the last month&nbsp;
and in particular in the last two weeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:56.320
things are looking dramatically different. We&nbsp;
mentioned yesterday the Senate has approved this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.000
Inflation Reduction Act bill to fight climate&nbsp;
change and cut drug costs. This is a major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.800
accomplishment. Assuming that the House passes&nbsp;
it on Friday and then it is signed by Joe Biden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:12.240
both of which are expected to happen.&nbsp;
This is a massive Biden accomplishment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:18.160
And then when you look bigger picture at the&nbsp;
Biden accomplishments, you see that he did the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:24.320
COVID stimulus, he did the Infrastructure and&nbsp;
Jobs Act. He confirmed the first black female&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:29.920
Supreme Court justice. He did some gun safety&nbsp;
legislation, although I think it's pretty weak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:36.640
sauce. But at least it was something he did.&nbsp;
The Chips Act for semiconductor manufacturing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:42.800
the NAITO expansion to include Finland and Sweden&nbsp;
is in process. He expanded veterans health care.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:50.320
He authorized the strike that killed terrorist&nbsp;
Ayman al-Zawahiri, which, believe me, I understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:55.120
there are legal questions about whether the&nbsp;
United States can or should be doing that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:01.200
but it is an accomplishment that Biden can&nbsp;
claim. Fantastic jobs report last week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:09.040
3.5% unemployment, 55 straight days of gas price&nbsp;
reduction, which again, remember, I don't even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:12.560
think it has anything to do with Biden. I don't&nbsp;
think the upswing had anything to do with Biden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.280
I don't think the downswing has anything to do&nbsp;
with Joe Biden either. But the point is what is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.880
reported and what can you take credit for? And&nbsp;
tomorrow we have an inflation number coming out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.640
which I expect to be significantly lower than&nbsp;
the peak numbers we saw over the last few months.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:33.200
I may be wrong, but that's what I expect. And&nbsp;
if that's the case, it will be another indicator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:40.800
that the economy is looking better and&nbsp;
better overall. Could this be a disastrous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:47.440
midterm for Republicans? Well, the polling&nbsp;
data is increasingly pointing that way. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:53.280
looking for months and months like Republicans&nbsp;
were going to take the Senate definitively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.280 --> 00:03:02.080
from Democrats in the fall. The FiveThirtyEight&nbsp;
forecast for the Senate now has Democrats at 59%,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:10.720
likely to retain control of the Senate. Now,&nbsp;
that's not overwhelming, but it is looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:17.280
increasingly good for Democrats in terms of the&nbsp;
Senate. Now, in the House, it's not looking very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:23.360
good. It still looks like about an 80% chance that&nbsp;
Republicans win. Remember, 80% is not 100%. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:29.360
that's the way that it is looking right now. This&nbsp;
is a massive, massive reversal from the way things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:34.160
looked and quite frankly, the way things should&nbsp;
look, speaking historically for Republicans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.440
What do you think we're going to see in&nbsp;
November? And then the last piece of this, as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:44.000
we spoke about this a little bit with political&nbsp;
scientist Rachel Bitter Copper last week. She has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.320
a slightly different view on it than I do. And I&nbsp;
know many of you have different views about this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:55.600
because of the overturning of Roe v Wade. This&nbsp;
actually does seem like it is a midterm election&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:01.760
where running on abortion rights, on women&nbsp;
having autonomy over their medical decisions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:06.800
could be very good for Democrats. Typically, it&nbsp;
is not an issue that is so good for Democrats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:13.040
Extraordinary circumstances. And as I've said&nbsp;
before, there are some elections which just don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:19.280
feel like they're that important. The 2022 midterm&nbsp;
and the 2024 presidential election, which are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.280
honestly one in the same. I mean, the 24 election&nbsp;
is almost getting going right now. And we're going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.600
to look at some of those numbers later as well,&nbsp;
because what is happening with Trump and de Santos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:34.160
is extraordinary. Could this be a disaster&nbsp;
for Republicans? Let me know what you think

